      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thank you! I was about to make a canny post for this same reason, it's very common to hit upload on content, and then leave it processing in the background. After all, depending on the content it can take a bit sometimes. It's incredibly frustrating to leave and come back, only to see that it didnt actually finish because the popup for copyright popped up.\n\nbecause it doesn't always pop up either. Why in the world was this changed from a checkbox? legally, it has about the same binding power, as long as it's there at all. This just seems like a change for the sake of making it more in your face. Which is fine, but perhaps put the pop up at the *start* of the process, instead of the very end.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
